<title>UK: Gecamines confirms cobalt airlift to Europe.</title>
<headline>Gecamines confirms cobalt airlift to Europe.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gecamines, the Democratic Republic of the Congo's state mining giant, confirmed it was airlifting cobalt from Lubumbashi to Europe to meet a contractual backlog.</p>
<p>In a statement faxed to Reuters, the company's London office said some 200 tonnes of the metal would be handled in this way in June and possibly more in July.</p>
<p>&quot;In order to meet contractual backlog, Gecamines confirms having adopted the alternative of airlifting cobalt from Lubumbashi to Europe,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>&quot;Therefore, about 200 tonnes will be handled in June and some other 100 tonnes in July if necessary.&quot;</p>
<p>Last month, a Gecamines marketing official was quoted as saying the company was airfreighting cobalt to Europe in order to benefit from high prices.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
